'''Arop-Lokep''' (also spelled '''Arop-Lukep''') is an [[Oceanic languages|Oceanic language]] spoken by 3,015 people ({{As of|2000|lc=on}}) on four islands in the [[Siassi chain]] in the [[Vitiaz Strait]] in [[Papua New Guinea]].

